<item>
            <title>[LU-20812] mdc: mdc_create() leaks the request on a bad mkdir reply</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20812</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In mdc_create(), after a successful reint for a directory, two error exits return before *request = req:&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - req_capsule_server_get(&amp;amp;RMF_MDT_BODY) returns NULL &#8594; RETURN(-EPROTO)&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - req_capsule_server_sized_get(&amp;amp;RMF_MDT_MD) returns NULL &#8594; RETURN(-EPROTO)&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
The caller never gets the request, so it is never put. The request leaks, and with it the import reference taken by ptlrpc_request_alloc(). A short or malformed mkdir reply from&#160;the MDT can trigger either one.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Fix: ptlrpc_req_put(req) before both returns, or set *request = req first so the caller&#160;drops it.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Found during review of &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/65026&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/65026&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20050&quot; title=&quot;ptlrpc: fix sepol error handling in ptlrpc_connect_import_locked&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20050&quot;&gt;LU-20050&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
